# Read-only host-side window-rectangle probe, 100 % form (adr/0018 section 5.2 row 3).
#
# WHAT IT DOES: joins the RAIL session a window-smoke run has just left behind -- the run must
# NOT log off (jobs/logoff-path.env is for between batches, not between a smoke run and this) --
# and asks Windows itself for every visible top-level window's GetWindowRect,
# DWMWA_EXTENDED_FRAME_BOUNDS, ClientToScreen(0,0), GetClientRect, GetDpiForWindow and the
# GetSystemMetricsForDpi frame/caption metrics. Nothing on the host is written, read or changed
# beyond that: no registry, no service, no elevation, one report back over the redirected drive.
# The report carries numbers, class names and process image names only -- never a window title
# (only its length and an 8-hex digest), never a user or computer name, never a path.
#
# OPERATOR ORDER. Consumed by relay.command through run-scenario.sh. The probe measures the
# windows a window-smoke run left behind, so it runs AFTER that run and BEFORE anything logs
# the session off:
#   Scripts/lab/run-scenario.sh smoke 1x-D                 # the run whose windows are measured
#   rm -f .build/lab-runtime/share/window-rects-out.txt    # the OPERATOR STEP below
#   Scripts/lab/run-scenario.sh relay window-rects-1x      # this job
# Do NOT run `Scripts/lab/run-scenario.sh relay logoff-path` between the two: logging off
# destroys the windows this job exists to measure. The 1x and 2x forms are two separate
# batches, each with its own smoke run; do not fold them into one session.
#
# WHY THE SCALE IS PINNED: the relay's connection declares its own TS_UD_CS_CORE
# desktopScaleFactor, and a client that joins a retained session with a DIFFERENT declared scale
# makes the server re-lay-out the session -- the windows whose rectangles are being measured
# would move and resize between the smoke run and this probe, and the measurement would be of a
# state that never existed during the run under study. /scale-desktop:100 pins this connection to
# the same 100 % the 1x smoke run declared. deviceScaleFactor is deliberately NOT passed, so it
# stays at FreeRDP's unconditional 100 -- product default D. relay.command admits
# /scale-desktop:<100-500> from its closed XFREERDP_EXTRA allowlist, so no relay change was
# needed for either form.
#
# Full path, not `||powershell`: the alias form resolves only against a published
# TSAppAllowList\Applications entry, and outside the matrix's Enforce window there is none (see
# jobs/server-snapshot.env for the full reasoning and the RAIL_EXEC_E_FILE_NOT_FOUND it earns).
#
# OPERATOR STEP before every launch: remove the previous report, e.g.
#   rm -f .build/lab-runtime/share/window-rects-out.txt
# The script rewrites it as a CHECKPOINT: started file before it enumerates anything, so a run
# that dies mid-probe cannot leave a complete previous report behind; a job the host refuses
# BEFORE the script starts writes nothing at all, and then only the missing file tells the truth.
# run-scenario.sh deliberately never removes host-written *-out.txt (see stage_share).
PROGRAM='C:\Windows\System32\WindowsPowerShell\v1.0\powershell.exe'
CMDARGS='-NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \\tsclient\lab\window-rects-probe.ps1'
XFREERDP_EXTRA='/scale-desktop:100'
# Bound. The probe is one Add-Type compile (a second or two on a cold .NET Framework csc), one
# EnumWindows pass and at most 64 rows of a dozen cheap user32/dwmapi calls each -- far under
# this. 60 s leaves room for the RAIL handshake and a cold compile without letting a hung call
# hold the connection open for minutes.
TIMEOUT=60
